25. Tap Zoom out on the map.
26. Tap the Account tab.
27. Tap Go online and wait until the page shows online before continuing.
28. Tap Open 1 request.
29. Tap Service city on the map.
30. Tap the Account tab.
31. Tap Go offline and wait until the page shows offline before continuing.
32. Tap Go online and wait until the page shows online again.
33. Swipe up on the Account page until the Driver onboarding form is visible.
34. Tap the D-2048 driver license input field.
35. Tap the Toyota vehicle make input field.
36. Tap the Camry vehicle model input field.
37. Tap the 2022 year input field.
38. Tap the DRV-204 license plate input field.
39. Tap the Blue color input field.
40. Tap the keyboard Done key to hide the keyboard.
41. Swipe down on the Account page back to the Availability area.
42. Tap the Money tab.
43. Tap the top Refresh button.
44. Swipe up on the Money page until the Payouts area is visible.
45. Swipe down on the Money page back to the Today and Total cards.
46. Tap the Money tab and keep the income page selected.
47. Swipe up on the Money page until Trip earnings is visible.
48. Swipe up on the Money page until Available payout information is visible.
49. Swipe down on the Money page back to the income summary top.
50. Tap Refresh.
51. Tap the Support tab.
52. Tap the customer support message input field.
53. Tap the keyboard Done key to hide the keyboard.
54. Tap Create support ticket.
55. Tap Refresh so the new ticket list refreshes.
56. Tap the Support tab.
57. Swipe up on the Support page until the newly appearing rider issue - open ticket is visible.
58. Tap Reply to ticket in the rider issue - open ticket.
59. Tap the Support tab to return to the support list area.
60. Tap Reply to ticket in the Payments - open ticket.
61. Tap the Support tab to return to the support list area.
62. Swipe down on the Support page back to the Driver safety and support top.
63. Tap the customer support message input field.
64. Tap the keyboard Done key to hide the keyboard.
65. Tap Refresh.
66. Tap the Support tab and finish on the support ticket list page containing rider issue - open.
